stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> OPEN: period opened, rule-set versions resolved
    OPEN --> INPUTS_CLOSED: close inputs, input snapshot frozen
    INPUTS_CLOSED --> OPEN: reopen, superseded snapshot kept
    INPUTS_CLOSED --> PROCESSED: results stamped with rule versions and evaluation context
    PROCESSED --> PROCESSED: reprocess, new result version, prior kept for diff
    PROCESSED --> APPROVED: checker approves, never the maker
    APPROVED --> PROCESSED: return for correction, approval voided
    APPROVED --> LOCKED: lock, every result immutable
    LOCKED --> DISBURSED: salaries released, actual disbursal date recorded
    DISBURSED --> PAYMENT_INITIATED: verification gate passed, challan with TRRN
    PAYMENT_INITIATED --> FILED: every monthly filing FILED
    FILED --> [*]

    LOCKED --> CORRECTION_RUN: change needed
    DISBURSED --> CORRECTION_RUN: change needed
    PAYMENT_INITIATED --> CORRECTION_RUN: change needed
    FILED --> CORRECTION_RUN: change needed
    CORRECTION_RUN --> OPEN: a new run that diffs against the locked snapshot

    state "Correction run - arrears, off-cycle or FnF" as CORRECTION_RUN

    note left of OPEN
        Specified as a transition table in 08 FR-PAY-301.
        This view shows what each state freezes in the data model.
        Every transition emits exactly one AuditEvent.
    end note

    note right of LOCKED
        Reversible before LOCKED.
        From LOCKED onward nothing is edited in place.
        A correction is a diff, never a mutation.
    end note

    note right of PAYMENT_INITIATED
        The statutory verification gate sits immediately before this state.
        After it a Revised ECR is impossible - EV-037.
    end note
